
                                               SPLITINFOBLOCK COMMAND


Splits input hex file based on infoblocks.

Below is the syntax :
              
              splitinfoblock        -infoblocknames [infoblock names | ALL]     
                                    -addr [start address]
                                    -dir [output directory]
                                    -type [output file type { IHEX/S19/BIN }]
                                    -lyt [output file layput]
                                     

--------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES                  |    DESCRIPTION
--------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   -infoblocknames        |    Infoblock names which should be written in seperate hex file
                          |    You can give ALL value to split all infoblocks. Mandatory switch.
   -addr                  |    Start address to perform blockbuild. OR perform blockbuild separately. Optional switch.
   -dir                   |    Output directory path. Default is present working directory. Optional switch.
   -type                  |    Output file type. Default type is IHEX. Optional switch. 
   -lyt                   |    Specifies the layout that the output hex file must be serialized with. Default layout of 0x10.
                          |    Optional switch.
--------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


Alternative switches:
                 
                 -infoblocknames   |   -ibnames, -infoblknames
                 -addr             |   -address
                 -lyt              |   -layout

Tip: 
    You can perform blockbuild operation separately using 'blkbuild' command and then perform infoblock split operation
    using 'splitinfoblock' command without giving '-addr' or '-address' command option. Refer Example(3)

Example:
        1)  read -in medc18.hex -type hex ^
            splitinfoblock -addr 0x80000020 -infoblocknames ALL -dir _out/infoblocks/
            
        2)  read -in medc18.hex -type hex ^
            splitinfoblock -addr 0x80000020 -infoblocknames CB,DS0,ASW1 -type bin -lyt 0x20

        3)  read -in medc18.hex -type hex ^
            blkbuild  -start 0x80000020 ^
            splitinfoblock -infoblocknames ALL -dir _out/infoblocks



